<section id="install" class="not-content">
  <h2>Install</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <p>Download the release archive for your host. The archive has one file: the program <code>mobius</code>.</p>
      <p>On an Apple silicon Mac:</p>
      <pre>rm -rf ~/.mobius/app && mkdir -p ~/.mobius/app
curl -fsSL https://github.com/Mobius-Toolkit/Mobius/releases/latest/download/mobius-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz \
  | tar -xz -C ~/.mobius/app</pre>
      <p>On Linux x86_64:</p>
      <pre>rm -rf ~/.mobius/app && mkdir -p ~/.mobius/app
curl -fsSL https://github.com/Mobius-Toolkit/Mobius/releases/latest/download/mobius-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz \
  | tar -xz -C ~/.mobius/app</pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>Add <code>~/.mobius/app</code> to <code>PATH</code> in your shell profile:</p>
      <pre>export PATH="$HOME/.mobius/app:$PATH"</pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>Make sure that the program starts:</p>
      <pre>mobius --help</pre>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Use <code>curl</code>, not a browser. macOS blocks an unsigned program that a browser downloads. <code>curl</code> does not mark the file.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mobius also needs other programs, for example <code>git</code> and <code>gh</code>. The install guide lists them.
  </p>
  <p class="links">
    <a href="https://github.com/Mobius-Toolkit/Mobius/blob/main/docs/install.md">Read the full install guide</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/Mobius-Toolkit/Mobius/releases">Releases on GitHub</a>
  </p>
</section>

